#78500
"A Small, Rough Cavern"
"A small cavern has been carved out of the very mountain itself.  The
stone is damp and covered with a fine layer of multicolored molds,
mildews, and moss.  The air has a slight chill to it and the pungent odor
of the flora on the stone can be detected.  The walls look quite old; and
an equally old looking set of stone stairs leads down into the darkness.
"
""
