#78507
"A Pathway in a Large Cavern"
"Leading to the north a hallway as been carved into the stone of the
cavern's wall.  The walls of the cavern shoot up into darkness,
preventing you from seeing the ceiling.  It appears that piles of rubble
have been used to partion off the cavern a great deal.  One such wall
prevents your movement south.  A worn, narrow path leads to the east and
west.  The air here is very dry and nothing seems to be growing on the
stone, with the exception of some dust bunnies.
"
""
